iven that $x=3{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}+5{b}_{3}.$" "$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\}$ to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\}$ is given above. Find $[x]_{C}$ given that $x=3{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}+5{b}_{3}.$"] [:db/cas 17592186394435 :question/worked-solution "First, notice that since $x=3{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}+5{b}_{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, notice that since $x=3{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}+5{b}_{3},$ we have\n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nGiven the coordinates of $x$ relative to $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C,$ we find the coordinates of $x$ relative to $C$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\,x\\,]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}[\\,x\\,]_{B} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186394437 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186394438 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186394439 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186394440 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}