n{aligned}5 & 1\\end{aligned}]+(-24)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 1\\end{aligned}]+(-24)\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}(2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 & 1\\end{aligned}]+(-24)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -5\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}(2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}25 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]+(-24)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 25\\end{aligned}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}[\\begin{aligned}26 & 130 \\\\ 130 & -598\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -23\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "The spectral decomposition of a $2\\times 2$ symmetric matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}^{T},\n$$\n\nwhere ${u}_{1}$ and ${u}_{2}$ are orthonormal eigenvectors of $A$ corresponding to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2},$ respectively.\n\nFirst, let's normalize our eigenvectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{{v}_{1}}{‖{v}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}_{2} & =\\frac{{v}_{2}}{‖{v}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\lambda }_{1}{u}_{1}{u}_{1}^{T}+{\\lambda }_{2}{u}_{2}{u}_{2}^{T} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+(-24)\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{26}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+(-24)\\cdot \\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}(2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+(-24)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}(2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}25 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+(-24)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ -5 & 25\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{26}\\begin{bmatrix}26 & 130 \\\\ 130 & -598\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -23\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186395075 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -18\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -18\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395076 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -23\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -23\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395077 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -17\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -17\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395078 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -21\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -21\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395079 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -17\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -17\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395081 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395082 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395083 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395084 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395085 :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]" "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}"] [:db/cas 17592186395086 :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$"] [:db/cas 17592186395086 :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}85 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 40\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=10$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=5.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=100,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-100I & =[\\begin{aligned}85 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 40\\end{aligned}]-100[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 & 30 \\\\ 30 & -60\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-100I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-25I & =[\\begin{aligned}85 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 40\\end{aligned}]-25[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}60 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 15\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 10\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}85 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 40\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: From the matrix $Σ,$ we deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=10$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=5.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=100,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-100I & =\\begin{bmatrix}85 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 40\\end{bmatrix}-100\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 30 \\\\ 30 & -60\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-100I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=25,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-25I & =\\begin{bmatrix}85 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 40\\end{bmatrix}-25\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}60 & 30 \\\\ 30 & 15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-25I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 10\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186395088 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186395089 :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{aligned}]$" "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{13}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{13}}\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/cas 17592186395090 :answer/value