gned}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\"" "A block lower triangular matrix can be partitioned so that it has only square blocks on the main diagonal, and the blocks above the main diagonal contain only zeros.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- $A$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $C$ is a block lower triangular matrix. Indeed, we can partition it as follows:\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A,$ $B,$ and $C.$\""] [:db/cas 17592186396694 :question/problem "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]?$" "The set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is linearly dependent. Which of the following vectors could be ${a}_{2}$ if\n${a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}?$"] [:db/cas 17592186396694 :question/worked-solution "We say that two vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nA set containing *only two* vectors is linearly *dependent* if and only if the two vectors are parallel.\n\nFrom the given options, the correct answer i